WEBVTT

00:02.085 --> 00:04.630
Our staff are currently
looking into the situation!

00:05.005 --> 00:08.217
Please remain where
you are and wait patiently!

00:08.800 --> 00:10.677
Aizawa? Where are you?

00:11.720 --> 00:14.138
What, you ran across a villain?

00:14.139 --> 00:17.767
That's why I won't be able
to make it to that event.

00:17.768 --> 00:19.603
Never mind that.
What's happening?

00:20.062 --> 00:22.063
I've apprehended the villain.

00:22.064 --> 00:25.526
No need for backup. I'm currently
waiting for the villain wagon.

00:26.360 --> 00:29.404
I guess they're going to
have to cancel the event?

02:00.329 --> 02:01.412
IDOL

02:01.413 --> 02:06.167
IDOL AN IMAGE OR REPRESENTATION OF AN OBJECT OF WORSHIP; A
PERFORMER WHO CAPITALIZES ON HIS OR HER CHARM AND PERSONALITY

02:06.168 --> 02:07.376
IDOL AN IMAGE OR REPRESENTATION OF AN OBJECT OF WORSHIP; A PERFORMER
WHO CAPITALIZES ON HIS OR HER CHARM AND PERSONALITY GOODBYE TO DAD

02:07.377 --> 02:08.378
GOODBYE TO DAD

02:09.171 --> 02:13.716
You're saying this blackout
was caused by a villain's Quirk.

02:13.717 --> 02:16.928
Well, Marukane's backup power
is only meant for emergency use.

02:16.929 --> 02:19.639
All the transformers in
the area were damaged.

02:19.640 --> 02:21.892
Looks like it'll take a
while to restore power.

02:22.392 --> 02:23.476
What now?

02:23.477 --> 02:28.148
If we got involved, it would be to
evacuate everyone, thus ending the show.

02:28.565 --> 02:30.192
Hey, Makoto!

02:30.484 --> 02:33.695
I flew straight here when I heard
there was an incident in Naruhata.

02:34.988 --> 02:36.865
Boss! I have an errand for you!

02:37.199 --> 02:40.661
Fine, but you never
give me a moment's rest.

02:41.328 --> 02:42.538
The show will go on!

02:42.871 --> 02:45.706
Until the boss comes back
with emergency generators,

02:45.707 --> 02:47.501
our MC will have to keep
the audience entertained.

02:47.835 --> 02:49.252
If you would, Mr. Mic.

02:49.253 --> 02:51.170
Sorry, no can do.

02:51.171 --> 02:53.840
We're officially required
to remain on standby

02:53.841 --> 02:56.677
until a situation like
this is fully under control.

02:57.928 --> 02:59.220
Now what?

02:59.221 --> 03:02.640
If I go onstage, I won't be able to
manage things behind the scenes.

03:02.641 --> 03:04.560
I guess we have to cancel?

03:05.602 --> 03:06.602
Huh?

03:06.603 --> 03:07.646
Where's Koichi?

03:08.230 --> 03:10.815
I'm the guy who
brought a surprise!

03:10.816 --> 03:11.858
The Crawler!

03:11.859 --> 03:12.901
Ouch!

03:13.902 --> 03:14.945
Ow, ow...

03:15.612 --> 03:16.779
A surprise?

03:16.780 --> 03:17.531
Pop.

03:17.823 --> 03:19.740
Here, it's the one
you always use!

03:19.741 --> 03:20.992
I went home and got it!

03:20.993 --> 03:23.954
She's always using
this for street shows,

03:24.288 --> 03:28.249
and for directing people to
safety during villain incidents.

03:28.250 --> 03:29.959
You're great at
this sort of thing.

03:29.960 --> 03:32.086
That's a big ask,
all of a sudden.

03:32.087 --> 03:33.672
Sure as hell is.

03:35.424 --> 03:38.635
Yeah, maybe I am
great at this sort of thing.

03:39.595 --> 03:43.890
I'll feed you updates and safety
precautions via this earpiece.

03:43.891 --> 03:45.516
Okay, Pop.

03:45.517 --> 03:48.562
You've got to keep the audience
occupied for thirty minutes at most.

03:49.563 --> 03:52.190
Starting now, you'll
be doing this solo.

03:52.191 --> 03:53.400
We're counting on you.

03:54.818 --> 03:55.902
Be strong.

03:55.903 --> 03:57.070
You got this.

03:57.404 --> 03:58.488
Please.

04:04.578 --> 04:05.704
Yeah!

04:07.372 --> 04:08.624
Yay!

04:09.458 --> 04:10.459
Dummy.

04:21.136 --> 04:22.930
Oguro speaking.

04:23.305 --> 04:25.682
This is Naruhata
General Hospital.

04:26.058 --> 04:27.643
Ahh, sorry.

04:28.060 --> 04:29.603
I'm on the move right now.

04:39.780 --> 04:41.990
No, it's no problem.

04:42.241 --> 04:43.449
What is this about?

04:43.450 --> 04:46.160
There's been a sudden change
in your wife's condition, and—

04:46.161 --> 04:47.537
All right.

04:47.538 --> 04:48.747
I understand.

04:49.623 --> 04:51.667
The whole family
will be there soon.

04:57.256 --> 05:00.216
Hey, if I could get
everyone's attention!

05:00.217 --> 05:02.552
I have some info
from the event staff!

05:02.553 --> 05:07.265
The power is out due to a villain
incident that occurred nearby,

05:07.266 --> 05:10.560
and they're working hard
to get things running again.

05:10.561 --> 05:14.230
Please wait where you are
until the lights come back on.

05:14.231 --> 05:20.027
In case you were wondering, I'm
Pop☆Step, an independent Naruhata idol!

05:20.028 --> 05:23.698
Usually you'd find me singing at
a street corner near the station,

05:23.699 --> 05:24.949
or in the neighborhood park,

05:24.950 --> 05:28.077
so some of you locals
may have seen me before.

05:28.078 --> 05:29.745
We'd never miss it!

05:29.746 --> 05:30.788
Thanks!

05:30.789 --> 05:34.375
But I'm always singing and
then leaving on my own schedule,

05:34.376 --> 05:39.297
so this might well be the first time
I've truly faced an audience this way.

05:39.298 --> 05:41.842
That's why right now,
my heart is pounding,

05:42.759 --> 05:45.554
and it feels like I need
to run to the bathroom.

05:46.722 --> 05:50.099
Oh, I just meant
that, like, emotionally!

05:50.100 --> 05:51.726
I made sure to go
right before this,

05:51.727 --> 05:53.853
so I can handle jumping
and bouncing around!

05:53.854 --> 05:57.565
Don't you think she's
getting a little weird?

05:57.566 --> 06:00.109
Yeah. She's usually all like,
"Idols never go to the bathroom."

06:00.110 --> 06:01.152
- Yeah. She's usually all like, "Idols never go to the bathroom."
- And so, I'm sure we'll all be fine, but just to be safe,

06:01.153 --> 06:04.906
And so, I'm sure we'll all
be fine, but just to be safe,

06:04.907 --> 06:08.075
I could use a favor from
my cheering section!

06:08.076 --> 06:12.079
I bet you brought those shiny things
you always have during my shows.

06:12.080 --> 06:13.164
Yeah!

06:13.165 --> 06:16.542
Could you hold those, and line up
along the edges of the audience?

06:16.543 --> 06:17.835
Yeah!

06:17.836 --> 06:19.504
Okay, thanks!

06:19.505 --> 06:21.839
If anyone out there has
to go to the bathroom,

06:21.840 --> 06:24.717
or if you find you
aren't feeling well,

06:24.718 --> 06:27.011
please move over
to those lines of light.

06:27.012 --> 06:28.679
Someone on staff
will assist you!

06:28.680 --> 06:30.389
Hey, good thinking.

06:30.390 --> 06:31.891
She's handling the crowd well.

06:31.892 --> 06:34.852
That's all the info I need
to pass along for now.

06:34.853 --> 06:39.065
Anyone who needs a bathroom break,
there's time now before the main event.

06:39.066 --> 06:40.609
As for everyone else...

06:43.612 --> 06:45.572
please listen to me sing!

06:47.032 --> 06:53.454
The rhythm of my beating heart

06:53.455 --> 07:00.044
Won't stop, so
hold my hand tight

07:00.045 --> 07:01.754
You are my destiny

07:01.755 --> 07:03.381
I knew it straight away

07:03.382 --> 07:06.592
I can tell that's the way it is

07:06.593 --> 07:08.177
You don't remember me

07:08.178 --> 07:09.887
I can't forget that day

07:09.888 --> 07:16.228
You're forever a
hero in my heart

07:18.063 --> 07:19.481
Another panic?

07:19.898 --> 07:22.233
No, that's the
audience cheering.

07:22.234 --> 07:23.484
They didn't cancel after all.

07:23.485 --> 07:24.193
- even right now - They
didn't cancel after all.

07:24.194 --> 07:25.237
...even right now

07:25.821 --> 07:27.613
You're still my
one and only hero

07:27.614 --> 07:30.867
- You're still my one and only hero - Oh
look, she managed to steal the show after all.

07:30.868 --> 07:32.159
- You're still my one and only
hero - Her singing's as bad as ever.

07:32.160 --> 07:32.577
Her singing's as bad as ever.

07:32.578 --> 07:33.411
I only have to spot that hoodie

07:33.412 --> 07:35.079
- I only have to spot that
hoodie - And yet, she's so cute.

07:35.080 --> 07:35.746
I only have to spot that hoodie

07:35.747 --> 07:36.873
- I only have to spot
that hoodie - It's not fair.

07:36.874 --> 07:38.499
- I only have to spot
that hoodie - It sure isn't.

07:38.500 --> 07:44.423
Just wearing it makes the
courage well up inside you

07:45.883 --> 07:47.925
P-Pop...

07:47.926 --> 07:48.718
Pop?

07:48.719 --> 07:52.263
Oh, she's that local
idol or whatever.

07:52.264 --> 07:53.724
Yeah, she's part of the event.

07:54.099 --> 07:55.726
You're a fan of hers, huh?

07:56.101 --> 07:58.896
Well, you'll get to cheer
her on another time.

08:05.819 --> 08:07.612
What was that "bee"?

08:07.613 --> 08:10.281
It was injecting some
fluid with its stinger?

08:10.282 --> 08:12.618
Or was it extracting it instead?

08:18.916 --> 08:20.959
Looks like checkmate.

08:21.376 --> 08:26.589
Knowing what I know of your
athletic ability and the street layout

08:26.590 --> 08:30.969
made it possible to
corner you into a dead end.

08:31.762 --> 08:34.473
You think you've
got me cornered?

08:43.190 --> 08:47.236
You plan to inject yourself with a
booster, then force your way past.

08:47.528 --> 08:52.616
But instead, it's going to
leave you incapable of escape.

08:52.991 --> 08:57.495
Bee user, your personality is formed
from a composite of the host's brain

08:57.496 --> 09:01.291
and the swarm of parasitic bees.

09:01.708 --> 09:05.586
Because of that, once Trigger weakens
your level of psychological control,

09:05.587 --> 09:08.422
your apian mission is
going to take a back seat

09:08.423 --> 09:11.510
to the emotions of the
host—those of Tamao Oguro.

09:12.344 --> 09:13.637
A concert?!

09:14.221 --> 09:17.056
Why're you wasting
your time playing music?!

09:17.057 --> 09:19.100
You've got better
things to do these days!

09:19.101 --> 09:20.560
What the hell're you thinking?!

09:20.561 --> 09:23.187
You don't know a
thing about me, Dad!

09:23.188 --> 09:24.814
Tamao! Listen to your—

09:24.815 --> 09:26.608
It's always like this with you!

09:26.900 --> 09:29.236
Your mother is the one
who's responsible for you!

09:30.445 --> 09:31.989
Nag, nag.

09:32.155 --> 09:34.199
Nag, nag! Shut up already!

09:34.533 --> 09:36.618
See to it she stops hanging
around with those fools!

09:37.077 --> 09:38.954
Apologize to your father.

09:48.964 --> 09:50.799
Dudes like him.

09:51.550 --> 09:53.302
What a pain, huh?

09:55.470 --> 09:57.931
You piss me off so
much, you old fart!

09:58.432 --> 10:00.474
Yes, Tamao. That's the way.

10:00.475 --> 10:04.604
We haven't talked father
to daughter in a while.

10:04.605 --> 10:08.650
Come to think of it, I've never
really given you a fair shot.

10:09.860 --> 10:12.613
You won't get excuses.
I've done lots of reflecting.

10:21.330 --> 10:24.374
A hit to your chest
will stop your heart!

10:25.209 --> 10:28.879
You can reflect once
you're dead, Dad!

10:29.838 --> 10:31.464
An Electric Quirk.

10:31.465 --> 10:33.799
I didn't know she
had that card to play.

10:33.800 --> 10:36.761
Strange that we'd
choose the same weapon.

10:36.762 --> 10:39.096
She's got ingenuity and flair.

10:39.097 --> 10:42.434
That's my... little girl!

10:47.481 --> 10:49.983
Great. Fried my right hand.

10:54.196 --> 10:57.658
Have a swell time in hell, Dad.

10:57.991 --> 11:00.994
SNACK BASUE

11:05.165 --> 11:06.458
I'm placing an order.

11:07.501 --> 11:10.796
The usual painkillers,
the usual amount.

11:15.050 --> 11:18.177
You already went
through the last batch?

11:18.178 --> 11:22.557
Using that stuff every day
will screw up your brain.

11:22.558 --> 11:25.309
Don't tell someone
how to have a good time.

11:25.310 --> 11:27.937
You know, you're right. Sorry.

11:27.938 --> 11:32.276
Also, I want you to get
me what's written on this.

11:33.652 --> 11:38.030
The hell's this?
Ingredients for poison gas?

11:38.031 --> 11:42.159
It attracts insects. I
need it for pest control.

11:42.160 --> 11:46.706
Huh, you don't say.
Not that I understand.

11:46.707 --> 11:48.624
One last thing.

11:48.625 --> 11:50.126
Just say the word.

11:50.127 --> 11:51.170
To the stun gun, add...

11:55.549 --> 11:58.427
Huh? What're you talkin' about?

12:08.645 --> 12:10.062
Okay, we have power.

12:10.063 --> 12:10.814
Pop.

12:11.648 --> 12:14.859
Everyone, thank you
for being so patient!

12:14.860 --> 12:21.074
The Naruhata Festival—a Marukane/C.C.
joint venture—is about to resume!

12:22.492 --> 12:27.831
The first song of the evening block is by
FeatherHATS, the Narufest special ensemble:

12:28.290 --> 12:31.543
The Marukane Department
Store Song Remix!

12:39.301 --> 12:40.801
How's it goin'?

12:40.802 --> 12:42.053
Come on down

12:42.054 --> 12:43.513
Hope you're doin' well

12:43.514 --> 12:44.764
Come on down

12:44.765 --> 12:50.562
Hope all y'all can make it

12:51.605 --> 13:02.114
Come on!

13:02.115 --> 13:03.324
Didja know?

13:03.325 --> 13:04.534
Have ya heard?

13:04.535 --> 13:07.411
Have ya have ya have ya?

13:07.412 --> 13:09.997
A department store that's
been around for a century

13:09.998 --> 13:13.000
But history and tradition
have had their day!

13:13.001 --> 13:19.423
Come on!

13:19.424 --> 13:19.632
MARUKANE - Come on!

13:19.633 --> 13:20.174
Come on!

13:20.175 --> 13:22.677
- Come on!
- Marukane was founded one hundred years ago.

13:22.678 --> 13:23.761
- Come on!
- I'd like today's young people to liven things up for us

13:23.762 --> 13:25.221
I'd like today's young
people to liven things up for us

13:25.222 --> 13:29.142
as we take our first step
into the next hundred years.

13:33.313 --> 13:34.146
Here we go!

13:34.147 --> 13:36.649
Circle & square

13:36.650 --> 13:39.360
Turn a corner
'round the round part

13:39.361 --> 13:41.946
But don't be a total square

13:41.947 --> 13:44.907
Take a trip, take a trip

13:44.908 --> 13:49.788
Go for it, go for it

13:52.249 --> 13:58.045
It's all yours for the taking

13:58.046 --> 13:58.964
Come on!

14:16.607 --> 14:18.566
MARUKANE

14:18.567 --> 14:22.904
Oh, the show's back on
despite all that trouble?

14:22.905 --> 14:24.531
Sounds like the
crowd's really into it.

14:24.948 --> 14:29.911
But that sorta thing truly
annoys me, so I'm gonna ruin it.

14:29.912 --> 14:32.748
Hey, don't be that way.

14:34.374 --> 14:36.292
You don't know when to quit.

14:36.293 --> 14:38.377
And how are you even alive?

14:38.378 --> 14:39.962
You some monster?!

14:39.963 --> 14:42.673
There's no need to be jealous.

14:42.674 --> 14:46.093
I know you belong up
there in that spotlight.

14:46.094 --> 14:49.597
You've lost your way and
ended up here for now,

14:49.598 --> 14:54.353
but you should go wherever
you want, whenever you want.

14:55.979 --> 14:58.689
Daddy's got your back.

14:58.690 --> 15:02.652
You can lay off the
weird lame-ass daddy act.

15:02.653 --> 15:05.029
Don't be stubborn, Tamao.

15:05.030 --> 15:10.160
Whatever the bees in your head try
to tell you, you already know the truth.

15:10.744 --> 15:15.958
There's no dad anywhere
in the world as great as me.

15:21.046 --> 15:24.215
There it is right there.

15:24.216 --> 15:26.385
It's such a pain when
you do that sorta thing.

15:30.264 --> 15:34.393
I was enjoying this body, so I
was taking pretty good care of it.

15:34.810 --> 15:36.519
But it doesn't matter anymore.

15:36.520 --> 15:40.691
Time to finish using it up,
then become the next me.

15:41.733 --> 15:45.279
And it's goodbye
to dear old... dad!

16:04.756 --> 16:07.217
She's not bluffing this time.

16:07.509 --> 16:11.346
Bomb bees and enough
current to fry her own body.

16:11.597 --> 16:17.311
Chances are, the backlash from her
next attack is going to kill my daughter.

16:17.811 --> 16:20.063
Ah...

16:20.981 --> 16:23.192
That's the way her
eyes looked that day.

16:23.567 --> 16:25.903
That cold look of
rejection stopped me.

16:26.153 --> 16:29.281
I just stood there, barking
like a frightened dog!

16:29.740 --> 16:33.660
Rooted to the spot and
unable to handle the situation.

16:35.120 --> 16:37.664
That's when I lost my baby girl.

16:39.041 --> 16:40.917
But things are different now.

16:40.918 --> 16:43.504
I can step forward,
no hesitation!

16:45.422 --> 16:46.839
I'll counterattack.

16:46.840 --> 16:51.386
It's a simple behavioral principle, drilled
into me through training and combat.

16:51.762 --> 16:52.930
Strike!

16:53.180 --> 16:57.059
It makes no difference who the
opponent is or what they're after!

16:58.560 --> 17:02.648
Good people, bad people,
loved ones, or hated enemies!

17:02.940 --> 17:07.694
It makes no difference at
all, just step in and strike!

17:10.364 --> 17:11.906
I'll get through!

17:11.907 --> 17:14.243
This time for sure!

17:23.544 --> 17:26.088
Damn... you!

17:27.089 --> 17:30.675
Have you got time
for talking, bee user?

17:30.676 --> 17:33.678
That stun gun hit must have
made your heart convulse

17:33.679 --> 17:36.514
and halted blood
flow to the brain.

17:36.515 --> 17:38.809
That body's about to die.

17:41.520 --> 17:46.190
That's right, give your heart
another shock to restart it.

17:46.191 --> 17:48.317
There's no other
way to save yourself.

17:48.318 --> 17:50.152
It's what I did.

17:50.153 --> 17:53.115
But I'm not gonna let you!

17:54.408 --> 17:57.910
If Tamao's host brain
stops functioning,

17:57.911 --> 18:01.164
it's gonna get awfully
hard for you to think clearly!

18:06.378 --> 18:11.800
You lose control of your swarm,
and it instinctively flees the dying hive.

18:17.431 --> 18:21.310
All that's left is a queen
bee that's lost her swarm.

18:21.810 --> 18:24.396
You can't even fly or think.

18:26.899 --> 18:28.817
You're nothing but a maggot.

18:31.904 --> 18:34.448
This is synthetic
attractant pheromone.

18:40.370 --> 18:42.998
And a candlelight
memorial, to boot.

18:44.124 --> 18:45.292
Now, then.

18:47.336 --> 18:48.921
Let's get back to it, Tamao.

18:49.671 --> 18:50.547
Huh?

18:51.256 --> 18:53.049
What're you talkin' about?

18:53.050 --> 18:56.052
You want me to add
an AED to the stun gun?

18:56.053 --> 18:58.931
Just make it so
they share a battery.

18:59.223 --> 19:01.808
I want to switch between
gear as quickly as possible.

19:03.101 --> 19:06.730
I'm afraid to ask, but what're
you going to do with this?

19:07.231 --> 19:10.400
I need to start and
stop some hearts.

19:11.902 --> 19:14.530
Okay, you got it.

19:16.281 --> 19:20.160
But I really do think you
should cut back on the drugs.

19:28.293 --> 19:29.503
We're going home.

19:30.838 --> 19:32.548
We're going home, Tamao!

19:36.134 --> 19:38.262
Your mother's waiting for us!

19:51.859 --> 19:53.526
He is now restrained.

19:53.527 --> 19:55.027
Thank you for your service.

19:55.028 --> 19:56.070
You got it.

19:56.071 --> 19:57.114
Let's go.

20:00.701 --> 20:02.411
Hey, what gives?

20:03.203 --> 20:08.082
Sorry, listen. Could we wait a
few minutes before I hand him over?

20:08.083 --> 20:09.250
Huh?

20:09.251 --> 20:12.795
I'll look after him until he
calms down a little more.

20:12.796 --> 20:13.547
All right...

20:13.922 --> 20:17.050
Or more like, they're
right at the good part.

20:19.261 --> 20:20.721
MARUKANE

20:31.857 --> 20:33.232
That was surprisingly good!

20:33.233 --> 20:35.194
No, it was great!

20:37.529 --> 20:39.572
You nailed it, FeatherHATS!

20:39.573 --> 20:40.740
They're so cute!

20:40.741 --> 20:42.241
Encore!

20:42.242 --> 20:44.118
That's one excited crowd.

20:44.119 --> 20:45.453
Excuse me.

20:45.454 --> 20:47.997
I'm Tsukauchi, with the
Quirk Crimes Division.

20:47.998 --> 20:49.750
Oh, hello.

20:51.043 --> 20:53.836
He's not an instant villain?

20:53.837 --> 20:54.713
Correct.

20:55.380 --> 20:58.466
I have my doubts about
him fitting the definition

20:58.467 --> 21:01.344
of "sudden drug-induced
Quirk rampage."

21:01.345 --> 21:04.055
Did he have any sort
of injector on him?

21:04.056 --> 21:05.139
No.

21:05.140 --> 21:07.851
Oh, but speaking of injection...

21:08.393 --> 21:09.560
A bee?

21:09.561 --> 21:13.147
Although I don't know if it's
directly related to what happened.

21:13.148 --> 21:15.525
No, I think there's
something to this.

21:15.526 --> 21:18.319
Multiple people testified
about being stung by an insect

21:18.320 --> 21:21.532
in that mass outbreak of
instant villains the other day.

21:22.324 --> 21:24.201
Records, records.

21:24.743 --> 21:26.619
Records are crucial.

21:26.620 --> 21:29.580
Other people's data
tastes as sweet as honey.

21:29.581 --> 21:31.500
Oh, there we go.

21:32.042 --> 21:34.377
Slowly it oozes.

21:34.378 --> 21:38.090
Like honey collecting
in a beehive.

21:42.219 --> 21:45.180
In the end, "all" become "one."

21:51.645 --> 21:53.021
Or something like that.

23:25.906 --> 23:27.950
Master has disappeared.

23:28.408 --> 23:31.119
All he left behind was
his Knuckleduster gear.

23:32.120 --> 23:35.040
Next time, "What a
Man Takes with Him."

23:35.791 --> 23:39.461
Even so, I'm going to
live on as a vigilante.
